  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The noise of the field equation>

    Lecture<nbsp>6: <math|\<Phi\><rsub|q>=<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>C<rsub|q>\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>+C<rsub|q>B<rsub|q-q<rsub|0>>>,
    a noisy measurement. Since <math|\<psi\><rsub|q>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*\<Phi\><rsub|\<infty\>>>,

    <\equation*>
      \<omega\><rsub|q>\<assign\>K<rsub|q>\<Phi\><rsub|q>-<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*\<psi\><rsub|q>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|q><around|[|B<rsub|q-q<rsub|0>>|]>:
    </equation*>

    the noise observable of Lecture<nbsp>5 is the <strong|filtered
    measurement noise>.

    <\lemma*>
      For convex <math|\<Psi\>>, <math|\<bbb-E\>*\<Psi\><around|(|\<omega\><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\>\<bbb-E\>*\<Psi\><around|(|B<rsub|q-q<rsub|0>>|)>>,
      whatever the interaction. So <math|\<zeta\><rsub|q>=C<rsub|q>*\<omega\><rsub|q>>
      has

      <\equation*>
        \<bbb-E\>*\<mathe\><rsup|u*\<zeta\><rsub|q><around|(|x|)>>\<leqslant\>exp
        <around*|(|<frac|u<rsup|2>|2>*<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*a<rsup|2><around|(|q|)>|)>,<space|2em><around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*a<rsup|2><around|(|q|)>\<lesssim\><sqrt|q>.
      </equation*>
    </lemma*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Proof: conditional Jensen. One line.

      <item><math|\<zeta\>> is not Gaussian, but it has the <strong|tails of
      the free field>, uniformly in <math|N> and in the interaction.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The field equation>

    Lecture<nbsp>5, forecast form, in this profile:
    <math|K<rsub|q<rsub|0>>\<psi\><rsub|q>+\<cal-F\><rsub|q><around|(|\<psi\><rsub|q>|)>=\<omega\><rsub|q>>,
    with the exact (unknown) force. Explicit force
    <math|<wide|\<cal-F\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q>=K<rsub|q>\<varrho\><rsub|q>+<frac|\<lambda\>|3>y<rsup|3>>,
    <math|\<psi\>=Y+Z>:

    <\equation*>
      <frame|<space|0.27em>K<rsub|q<rsub|0>>Y<rsub|q>+<wide|\<cal-F\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>=\<omega\><rsub|q>+<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*Z<rsub|q><space|0.27em>>
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Elliptic at each <math|q>, <strong|no memory>, <strong|pathwise>;
      coercivity from the explicit <strong|cube>.

      <item>The backward equation enters only through
      <math|<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*Z<rsub|q>>.

      <item>Pointwise bounds need a smooth noise:
      <math|\<zeta\>=C<rsub|q>\<omega\>>, <math|V=Y+\<varrho\><around|(|Y|)>-\<zeta\>>,

      <\equation*>
        K<rsub|q<rsub|0>>*V<rsub|q>+<frac|\<lambda\>|3>*Y<rsub|q><rsup|3>=<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*<around|(|\<zeta\><rsub|q>-\<varrho\><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>+Z<rsub|q>|)>.
      </equation*>

      Mass only <math|q<rsub|0>>: all the coercivity comes from the cube.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Thresholds and energies>

    Thresholds: <math|w<rsub|q>=<math-up|sgn><around|(|V<rsub|q>|)>*<around*|(|<around|\||V<rsub|q>|\|>-<tfrac|3|4>r<rsub|q>|)><rsub|+>,<space|2em>t<rsub|q>=Y<rsub|q>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|<around|\||Y<rsub|q>|\|>\<gtr\>r<rsub|q>>,<space|2em>\<xi\><rsub|q>=\<zeta\><rsub|q>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|<around|\||\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\|>\<gtr\>r<rsub|q>/32>>.

    <\equation*>
      <\aligned>
        <tformat|<table|<row|<cell|E<rsub|T>>|<cell|=<tfrac|1|\<lambda\>><big|int>q<rsup|1/2><around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q<space|2em><text|backward
        energy>>>|<row|<cell|J<rsub|T>>|<cell|=<big|int>q<rsup|-3/2>*<around*|[|q*<around|\<\|\|\>|w<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|4><rsup|4>+\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|w<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>+\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>|]>\<mathd\>q<space|2em><text|large-field
        action>>>|<row|<cell|G<rsub|T>>|<cell|=<big|int><around*|[|q<rsup|-1/2>*<around|\<\|\|\>|\<xi\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|4><rsup|4>+\<lambda\>*q<rsup|-3/2><around|\<\|\|\>|\<xi\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>|]>\<mathd\>q<space|2em><text|noise
        tails>>>>>
      </aligned>
    </equation*>

    <data-table|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|quantity>|<cell|weight>|<cell|reason>>|<row|<cell|<math|<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>>|<cell|<math|q<rsup|1/2>>>|<cell|forcing:
    <math|q<rsup|-3/2>\<cdot\>\<lambda\><rsup|-1>*q<rsup|2><around|\<\|\|\>|Z|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2>>>>|<row|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>>>|<cell|<math|q<rsup|-3/2>>>|<cell|<math|q<rsup|7/2><around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|l>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>C*\<lambda\><rsup|3>\<cdot\>\<lambda\>*q<rsup|-3/2><around|\<\|\|\>|t|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>>>>|<row|<cell|<math|<around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|l>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>>|<cell|<math|q<rsup|7/2>>>|<cell|propagator
    <math|s/q>, <math|<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-3/2>=2*q<rsup|-1/2>>>>>>>

    Only <strong|thresholded> sixth powers:
    <math|\<bbb-E\><around|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>\<sim\>q<rsup|3/2>>
    would give <math|G<rsub|T>\<sim\>\<lambda\>*N<rsup|2>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <cqft-part-title|Forward coercivity>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture<nbsp>7>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The scalar model>

    <\lemma*>
      <dueto|scalar forward coercivity>If <math|a\<geqslant\>0>,
      <math|0\<leqslant\>p\<leqslant\>q> and
      <math|a*v+<frac|\<lambda\>|3>*<around|(|v+g|)><rsup|3>=p*<around|(|g+z|)>>,
      then, with <math|r=<around|(|q/\<lambda\>|)><rsup|1/2>>,

      <\equation*>
        <frac|q|8>*w<rsup|4>+<frac|\<lambda\>|16>*w<rsup|6>\<leqslant\>54*q*\<xi\><rsup|4>+<frac|4225|6>*\<lambda\>*\<xi\><rsup|6>+<frac|12|\<lambda\>>*q<rsup|2>*z<rsup|2>,
      </equation*>

      where <math|w=sgn<around|(|v|)>*<around|(|<around|\||v|\|>-<frac|3|4>*r|)><rsub|+>>,
      <math|\<xi\>=g*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|<around|\||g|\|>\<gtr\>r/32>>;
      and <math|<around|\||t|\|>\<leqslant\><frac|32|7>*<around|(|<around|\||w|\|>+<around|\||\<xi\>|\|>|)>>.
    </lemma*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>The excess is controlled <strong|at each resolution separately>
      by the noise tails and by the error <math|Z>.

      <item>No smallness of the coupling, and no integration in <math|q>:
      multiply by <math|q<rsup|-3/2>> only to match the energies.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Proof: test with <math|w<rsup|3>>>

    Where <math|w\<neq\>0>: <math|<around|\||v|\|>=<around|\||w|\|>+<frac|3|4>*r>,
    same sign, so <math|a*v*w<rsup|3>\<geqslant\>0>.

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Cube.> <math|sgn<around|(|w|)>*<around|(|v+g|)>\<geqslant\><around|\||w|\|>+<frac|11|16>*r-<around|\||\<xi\>|\|>>,
      and <math|\<lambda\>*r<rsup|2>=q>:

      <\equation*>
        <frac|\<lambda\>|3>*w<rsup|3>*<around|(|v+g|)><rsup|3>\<geqslant\><frac|\<lambda\>|12>*w<rsup|6>+<frac|q|4>*w<rsup|4>+<frac|q*r|13><around|\||w|\|><rsup|3>-<frac|4225|6>*\<lambda\>*\<xi\><rsup|6>.
      </equation*>

      <item><strong|Noise.> <math|p*g*w<rsup|3>\<leqslant\><frac|q*r|32><around|\||w|\|><rsup|3>+q<around|\||\<xi\>|\|><around|\||w|\|><rsup|3>>:
      the first term is absorbed by the cube, and
      <math|q<around|\||\<xi\>|\|><around|\||w|\|><rsup|3>\<leqslant\><frac|q|8>*w<rsup|4>+54*q*\<xi\><rsup|4>>.

      <item><strong|Error.> <math|q<around|\||z|\|><around|\||w|\|><rsup|3>\<leqslant\><frac|\<lambda\>|48>*w<rsup|6>+<frac|12|\<lambda\>>*q<rsup|2>*z<rsup|2>>.
    </itemize>

    <\myframed>
      Above the threshold the cube provides a sixth power, a mass <math|q>
      and a cubic term which dominates the noise below the threshold.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Two elementary inequalities>

    For <math|x,\<rho\>,u,r\<geqslant\>0>:

    <\equation*>
      <around|(|x-\<rho\>|)><rsup|3>\<geqslant\><frac|3|4>*x<rsup|3>-65*\<rho\><rsup|3>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      <frac|1|3>*u<rsup|3>*<around*|(|u+<frac|11|16>*r-\<rho\>|)><rsup|3>\<geqslant\><frac|1|12>*u<rsup|6>+<frac|1|4>*r<rsup|2>*u<rsup|4>+<frac|1|13>*r<rsup|3>*u<rsup|3>-<frac|4225|6>*\<rho\><rsup|6>.
    </equation*>

    <strong|Proof.> <math|<frac|1|4>*x<rsup|3>+64*\<rho\><rsup|3>-3*x<rsup|2>*\<rho\>=<frac|1|4>*<around|(|x-8*\<rho\>|)><rsup|2>*<around|(|x+4*\<rho\>|)>\<geqslant\>0>.
    Then <math|x=u+b>, <math|b=<frac|11|16>*r>:
    <math|<frac|3|4>*b<rsup|2>\<gtr\><frac|1|4>*r<rsup|2>>,
    <math|<frac|1|4>*b<rsup|3>\<gtr\><frac|1|13>*r<rsup|3>>, and
    <math|<frac|65|3>*u<rsup|3>*\<rho\><rsup|3>\<leqslant\><frac|1|6>*u<rsup|6>+<frac|4225|6>*\<rho\><rsup|6>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The lattice version>

    <\proposition*>
      <dueto|forward coercivity>For <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>> large, at every
      <math|N>, pathwise and for every <math|q>,

      <\equation*>
        q<around|\<\|\|\>|w<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|4><rsup|4>+\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|w<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>+\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>\<leqslant\>C*<around*|(|q<around|\<\|\|\>|\<xi\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|4><rsup|4>+\<lambda\><around|\<\|\|\>|\<xi\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>+\<lambda\><rsup|-1>*q<rsup|2><around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2>|)>.
      </equation*>

      So <math|J<rsub|T>\<leqslant\>C*<around|(|G<rsub|T>+E<rsub|T>|)>>, and
      <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|G<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>\<leqslant\>C*\<lambda\><rsup|3>*p<rsup|5>>.
    </proposition*>

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Elliptic term:> <math|w<rsup|3>=\<phi\><rprime|'><around|(|V|)>>,
      <math|\<phi\>> convex, so <math|<around|\<langle\>|w<rsup|3>,K<rsub|q<rsub|0>>*V|\<rangle\>>\<geqslant\>0>.

      <item><strong|Coordinate correction:>
      <math|\<varrho\>=\<varrho\><rsup|0>+\<varrho\><rsup|1>>,
      <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<varrho\><rsup|0>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<leqslant\>\<varepsilon\>*r>
      shifts the threshold, <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<varrho\><rsup|1>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|j>\<leqslant\>C*\<varepsilon\>*<around|(|<around|\<\|\|\>|w|\<\|\|\>><rsub|j>+<around|\<\|\|\>|\<xi\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|j>|)>>
      is absorbed.

      <item><strong|Noise tails:> <math|\<bbb-P\><around|(|<around|\||\<zeta\><rsub|q><around|(|x|)>|\|>\<gtr\>r<rsub|q>/32|)>\<leqslant\>2*\<mathe\><rsup|-c<sqrt|q>/\<lambda\>>>,
      by the lemma.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|<math|L<rsup|\<infty\>>> coercivity>

    <\proposition*>
      For <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>> large, at every <math|N>, pathwise and for
      every <math|q>,

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|Y<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<leqslant\>C*<around*|[|<around*|(|<frac|q|\<lambda\>>|)><rsup|1/3><around|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>><rsup|1/3>+<around|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>+q<rsup|1/4>+q<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2>|]>.
      </equation*>

      So <math|t<rsub|q>=0> whenever <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>+q<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2>\<leqslant\>c*r<rsub|q>>.
    </proposition*>

    <\itemize>
      <item>Remove the error: <math|\<cal-H\>=<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>*C<rsub|q<rsub|0>>*Z<rsub|q>>,
      with <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-H\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<lesssim\>q<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2>>.

      <item>At a maximum of <math|W=V-\<cal-H\>>, the elliptic term has a
      sign: <math|<frac|\<lambda\>|3>*Y<rsup|3>\<leqslant\>q<around|\<\|\|\>|d|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>>.
      <strong|The cube alone gives the bound.>

      <item><strong|Large fields occur only when the noise or the error is
      large.>

      <item>With <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|\<zeta\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|1/4>>
      and <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-5/4>>
      (Doob on <math|\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*A<rsup|<math-up|l>>>):
      <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|Y<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|5/12>\<ll\>r<rsub|q>>,
      up to logarithms.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <cqft-part-title|Backward feedback and closure>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture<nbsp>7>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The backward representation>

    \;

    Propagator: <math|\<partial\><rsub|s>*\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>=\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>*H<rsub|s><around|(|Y<rsub|s>|)>>,
    <math|\<cal-P\><rsub|q,q>=I>, and by (A)

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>L<rsub|0>*<space|0.17em><frac|s|q>,<space|2em>L<rsub|0>=exp
      <around*|(|<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|\<infty\>>\<varepsilon\><rsub|u>*<frac|\<mathd\>u|u>|)>\<leqslant\>\<mathe\><rsup|C*<around|(|g<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>+g<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|2>|)>>.
    </equation*>

    <\lemma*>
      <dueto|conditional representation>

      <\equation*>
        Z<rsub|q>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*<around*|[|\<cal-P\><rsub|q,T>*Z<rsub|T>+<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|T>\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>*<space|0.17em>b<rsub|s><around|(|Y<rsub|s>|)><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>s|]>.
      </equation*>
    </lemma*>

    Proof: <math|\<mathd\><rsub|s><around|(|\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>*Z<rsub|s>|)>=-\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>*b<rsub|s>\<mathd\>s+\<cal-P\><rsub|q,s>*\<Xi\><rsub|s>\<mathd\>W<rsub|s>>,
    a true martingale at fixed <math|N>.

    <math|Z> = expected source on the unresolved scales, transported back,
    plus the boundary error. Compare <math|F<rsub|t>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|t><around|[|F<rsub|T>|]>>
    in Lecture<nbsp>4: here the source is the <strong|defect>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Three contributions>

    \;

    <with|font-series|bold|Bounded fields> (two correction steps!):

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|<math-up|b>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>L<rsub|0>*<frac|s|q>*<space|0.17em>C*\<lambda\><rsup|7/2>*s<rsup|-5/2>\<mathd\>s=2*C*L<rsub|0>*\<lambda\><rsup|7/2>*q<rsup|-3/2>,<space|2em><tfrac|1|\<lambda\>><big|int>q<rsup|1/2><around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|<math-up|b>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>C*\<lambda\><rsup|6>*q<rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|-3/2>.
    </equation*>

    <with|font-series|bold|Boundary:> <math|q<around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|<math-up|t>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>>\<leqslant\>L<rsub|0>*\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*<around|\<\|\|\>|T*Z<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>>>,
    contributing <math|<frac|2*L<rsub|0><rsup|2>|\<lambda\>*q<rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/2>>*\<delta\><rsub|N,T,p>>,
    <math|\<delta\><rsub|N,T,p>=<around|\<\|\|\>|T*Z<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2><rsub|L<rsup|2*p>*<around|(|\<bbb-P\>;L<rsup|2>|)>>>.

    <with|font-series|bold|Large fields:>
    <math|A<rsup|<math-up|l>>=<big|int>s<rsup|7/2><around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|l>><rsub|s>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>C*\<lambda\><rsup|3>*J<rsub|T>>;
    Cauchy\USchwarz and Jensen,

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|<math-up|l>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>\<leqslant\>2*L<rsub|0><rsup|2>*q<rsup|-5/2>*\<bbb-E\><rsub|q>*A<rsup|<math-up|l>>,<space|2em><around*|\||<tfrac|1|\<lambda\>><big|int>q<rsup|1/2><around|\<\|\|\>|Z<rsup|<math-up|l>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>|\|><rsub|L<rsup|p>>\<leqslant\><frac|C*\<lambda\><rsup|2>|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><around|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      <strong|This is how the clipping error is controlled>

      <math|b<rsup|<math-up|l>>> is not small, but it enters the backward
      energy only through the large-field action <math|J<rsub|T>>, with the
      small factor <math|\<lambda\><rsup|2>/q<rsub|\<ast\>>>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Closing the loop>

    \;

    <\theorem*>
      <dueto|cutoff-uniform energy estimate>One
      <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>=q<rsub|\<ast\>><around|(|\<lambda\>|)>>: for all
      <math|N>, <math|T>, <math|p\<geqslant\>1>,

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|E<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>+<around|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|p>>\<leqslant\>C<rsub|\<lambda\>>*<around|(|1+p<rsup|5>+\<delta\><rsub|N,T,p>|)>.
      </equation*>
    </theorem*>

    <math|x=<around|\<\|\|\>|E<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p>>,
    <math|y=<around|\<\|\|\>|J<rsub|T>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p>>:<space|1em><math|y\<leqslant\>A<rsub|0>*<around|(|C*\<lambda\><rsup|3>*p<rsup|5>+x|)>>,
    <space|1em><math|x\<leqslant\>B<rsub|0>+B<rsub|1>*\<delta\>+\<theta\>*y>,
    <space|1em><math|\<theta\>=C*\<lambda\><rsup|2>/q<rsub|\<ast\>>=C*g<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>><rsup|2>>.
    Choose <math|A<rsub|0>*\<theta\>\<leqslant\><frac|1|2>>;
    <math|y\<less\>\<infty\>> at fixed <math|N,T>, absorb.

    <with|par-mode|center|<\script-output|tikz|default>
    \\documentclass[tikz]{standalone}

    \\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

    \\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}

